Root cause:
The bug was caused by a memory leak in the `of_overlay_apply()` function when `of_resolve_phandles()` failed. The `free_overlay_changeset()` function was called to clean up resources, but it did not properly handle the case where the `overlay_changeset` was only partially initialized. Specifically, it would return early if the list of changes had not been initialized, leading to allocated memory not being freed. This oversight resulted in a memory leak, as the allocated resources were not released when an error occurred during the initialization process. The patch addresses this by modifying `free_overlay_changeset()` to safely handle the cleanup of partially initialized objects.
